# Citation File Format 1.2.0 -- https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# `preferred-citation` is what you should cite in a publication: the peer
# reviewed article that describes the instrument.  The top-level entry
# describes this repository, and is what a data-availability statement should
# point at.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you build this instrument or use these files, please cite the article in
  `preferred-citation`.  If you need to cite the repository itself as well,
  cite the software entry below.
title: Low-Cost Rotational Viscometer (LC-RV)
abstract: >-
  Open hardware, firmware and analysis software for a 3D-printed
  concentric-cylinder (Couette) rotational viscometer that costs about $90 to
  build.  A stepper-driven bob rotates inside a stationary cup that is free to
  pivot on a bearing; a load cell holds the cup and reads the restraining
  force F.  With the wetted cup-wall area A the shear stress is F/A, and with
  the narrow-gap shear rate omega*R_b/G that gives viscosity over 5-400 RPM.
type: software
date-released: "2026-08-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/priye19/Low-cost---rotational-viscometer"
url: "https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jchemed.4c01490"
